; MX4 the string forms (docs/v35s-mechanisms.md section 3's string row; README "MX4"): MOVBK
; (A4 / A5), CMPBK (A6 / A7), STM (AA / AB), LDM (AC / AD), CMPM (AE / AF), INM (6C / 6D), OUTM
; (6E / 6F), single and under a REP prefix (F3 REP / REPE, F2 REPNE, 65 REPC, 64 REPNC). The
; source DS0:IX (a prefix's segment), the destination DS1:IY, the port DW; the width the format's
; (the opcode's bit 0, the second level's under a prefix); every element's index steps by the
; width, down with PSW.DIR set (AL_STEP). A REP form is the 0F page's structure: the E word pops
; the string opcode behind the prefix with it (into the ModR/M register) and the dispatch reads
; the second level on it; the prefix's own word is the routine's first (CW read for the zero
; test, the V20's JMP Z first). The count is CW in the register RAM (16 bits: the loop counter's 9
; do not hold it): each element's word decrements it through the ALU and writes it back, the
; next word tests SIGMA (CD_SNZ: the count ran out); a compare tests its result's condition
; first (CD_XC on the prefix's condition: Z for REPE, NZ for REPNE, CY for REPC, NC for REPNC).
; A REP compare posts the next element's read(s) before its tests take effect (silicon's
; overrun: F24 t-series, every REP compare that ran an element reads one more). Clocks in the
; comments: c<k> from the E word that popped the opcode (c0; the dispatch c1; the routine's first
; word c2), q the element's first post. The book is each routine's first draft (`book=` /
; `bookx=` the REP note's formula plus the prefix's 2); the clocks beyond it or short of it are
; silicon's (the frozen model exact on the runs named), OPEN words where no act names a clock.
; A run of OPEN clocks is one word calling the shared delay (`dly`: K OPEN words and a return)
; or a jump into the shared tails (`xb` / `xe`: K OPEN words and the E word).

; ---- the shared delay and tails (no opcode): OPEN words only
routine dly why="OPEN: the shared delay: a word's call=wK runs K OPEN clocks here and returns to the word after it (the book's clocks with no act of the routine that calls)"
w24: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w23: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w22: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w21: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w20: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w19: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w18: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w17: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w16: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w15: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w14: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w13: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w12: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w11: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w10: open                                   ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w9: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w8: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w7: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w6: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w5: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w4: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w3: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w2: open                                    ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's)
w1: open ret                                ; OPEN: a book clock with no act (the caller's); back to the caller's next word

; the string forms' exits: K OPEN clocks, then E with the write-back flag (a REP form's last
; register writes, CW and the index, run on past E: MX1f's wb; the frozen model's str_exit=wb /
; str_single_wb, xwb 2: only a successor that waits for a write-back sees the clocks)
routine sxt why="OPEN: the string forms' shared tails: the exit's book clocks with no act, then E (the caller's routine names its run)"
xb12: open call=w12                         ; OPEN: the compares' exit: thirteen book clocks with no act (the call and the shared delay's 12)
    open                                    ; OPEN: the write-back's second clock before E
    e                                       ; E: pop the next opcode; the index / count write-back runs on past E (wb)
; a REP compare's exits: the overrun read issued on the clock before (q + 10), its datum waited
; for (F: the W clocks: the datum's clock at q + 13 at W = 0 on either path), E 18 (+ W) clocks
; after its issue on the condition's exit and 19 on the count's. (qprobe round 18, Q80, spec 14 B2)
; Silicon: from the last read to the next instruction 26 clocks when the condition ended the loop
; (at any element, the last one too) and 27 when the count did: the count's exit one word longer
; behind the datum (sx_w's word), the tail two words shorter than round 12's (whose F word,
; reached on q + 13 by both paths, gave both exits the same length: 28)
sx_c: f jmp=xb12                            ; F: the overrun's datum (discarded); the tail
sx_w: f                                     ; F: the overrun's datum (discarded)
    open jmp=xb12                           ; OPEN: the count's exit's word with no act; the tail

; (qprobe round 12, spec 7 A3) the REP prefixes (F3 REP / REPE, F2 REPNE, 65 REPC, 64 REPNC) are their own two-word
; routine, as a segment prefix: the E word pops the string opcode into the REP page (ea=REP: the
; loader keeps the prefix in the opcode register and loads the popped byte into the ModR/M
; register, F5d's mechanism), so the string's boundary is a dispatch with the boundary's waits (a
; fetch in flight, the bytes behind the staged opcode); nb: no interrupt between the prefix and
; its instruction (the prefix's offset stays the start)
routine rep_p op=F2,F3,64,65 page=rep why="(qprobe round 12, spec 7 A3) the REP prefix is its own routine of two words (the qprobe rep runs: the string's head 14 words from c4, the zero exit 12)"
    e nb ea=REP                             ; E: the string opcode into the REP page; nb: no boundary for an interrupt (the prefix's offset kept: pist)

; (qprobe round 12, spec 8 A2 / spec 9 C1) a REP string broken between iterations: the take
; point (TKI) enters this exit, whose acknowledge's first cycle is 48 clocks after the last
; write's end at W = 0 (an unbroken boundary's is 16): about 30 words of exit in front of the
; interrupt entry (silicon's broken exit; the mechanism behind its length is not read)
routine rep_brk why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 12, Q41.3) a broken REP's exit: the acknowledge 48 clocks after the last write's end (the qprobe irep / jrep runs)"
    open call=w24                           ; OPEN: the broken REP's exit (the call and the shared delay's 24)
    open call=w2                            ; OPEN: the broken REP's exit (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    jmp=intr_k                              ; the interrupt entry (the acknowledge: INT 3's sequence); (WO39) the take point's (a DMA transfer refetches the string)

; ---- the single forms (no prefix): the element once. Clocks from the steady instance (the k2
; runs' second form, the frozen model exact): its first cycle's post at c7 / c8 / c9 / c10
routine movbk op=A4,A5 book="MOVBK" diff=1 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) MOVBK is `. . . . . Y D . . . Z DN .` (the qprobe movb / movw runs): the source's address, four words with no act, Y (the request word), IX stepped and the destination's address under the wait, the read's post, F (D: the datum into the write datum), IY stepped, two words with no act, the write's post (Z, four words after the datum), F with E (D N: the write's end, not its first clock) (WO47, build/overseer/ramen-design3 DESIGN3.md; at RAMEN 1 every clock as before: the access wait is the F word it replaced, a p0 word and the words under an access run inside the cycle) OPEN at RAMEN 0, a word count read from the pins: two words under the source read (2 words), the datum taken three words in front of the write's post; the read's F an access wait (fa); no early end (silicon keeps E on the write's first clock): the read to the second cycle 8 / 8 / 9 clocks at 0 / 1 / 2 waits; why silicon has the words is not known"
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the source's address IX
    open call=sb3                           ; OPEN: (r25, work order 21 B4, Q121) four words, the fourth bus-idle (`. . . B . Y`: zz_late.uasm sb3)
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IX + the width
    wr=IX ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IX stepped
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                        ; post the source read (Y + 3; its address taken at the grant: the address register kept until the datum)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47) a word under the access (with RAMEN 1 it runs inside the cycle, in front of the access wait)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47) a word under the access (with RAMEN 1 it runs inside the cycle, in front of the access wait)
    fa                                      ; (WO47) the access wait (RAMEN 1 only): the datum is taken two words on
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA alu=STEP ax=RA ; the destination's address IY; SIGMA = IY + the width
    wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD f d1=OPRW s1=OPR  ; IY stepped; (WO47) F: the datum wait: the datum into the write datum (three words in front of the write's post)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act ((WO47) no early end here: silicon's MOVBK keeps its E on the write's first clock at RAMEN 0, only F's wait goes)
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1                        ; Z: post the destination write (the datum + 5)
    f e ro                                  ; D N: F: the write's end; E; ro: released

routine cmpbk op=A6,A7 book="CMPBK" width=word diff=0 why="OPEN: book error of one (F24-out-s-cmpbk-w-k2-pE-w0); (qprobe round 11, Q34) CMPBK is `. . . . . Y D . . . U D . N .` (the qprobe cmpbk runs): [IY] first, then [IX]: the destination's address, four words with no act, Y, IY stepped and the source's address under the wait, the read's post, F (D), IX stepped, two words with no act, the second read's post (U, Z's timing: four words after the datum), F (D), the compare, E (WO47, build/overseer/ramen-design3 DESIGN3.md; at RAMEN 1 every clock as before: the access wait is the F word it replaced, a p0 word and the words under an access run inside the cycle) OPEN at RAMEN 0, a word count read from the pins: two words under the destination read (2 words), its F an access wait (fa), the datum taken two words on; the source's F carries the early end (ee: with RAMEN 0 the compare is the dispatch word, as CMP mem,reg's); why silicon has the words is not known"
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the destination's address IY (CMPBK reads it first)
    open call=sb3                           ; OPEN: (r25, work order 21 B4, Q121) four words, the fourth bus-idle (`. . . B . Y`: zz_late.uasm sb3)
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IY + the width
    wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IY stepped
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1                        ; post the destination read (Y + 3; the address register kept until the datum)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47) a word under the access (with RAMEN 1 it runs inside the cycle, in front of the access wait)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47) a word under the access (with RAMEN 1 it runs inside the cycle, in front of the access wait)
    fa                                      ; (WO47) the access wait (RAMEN 1 only): the datum is taken two words on
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA alu=STEP ax=RA ; the source's address IX; SIGMA = IX + the width
    wr=IX ws=SIG wid=WORD f d1=TB s1=OPR    ; IX stepped; (WO47) F: the datum wait: the destination's datum into tmpb
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                        ; U: post the source read (the datum + 5)
    f ee d1=TA s1=OPR                       ; D: F: the source's datum into tmpa; (WO47) ee: the early end (with RAMEN 0 the compare is the dispatch word, as CMP mem,reg's)
    alu=GRP ax=TA ay=TB wf                  ; the compare [IX] - [IY] (W)
    e ro                                    ; E (N); ro: released

routine stm op=AA,AB book="STM" diff=2 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) STM is `. . B . . . Y G N .` (the qprobe stmb / stmw runs): the destination's address, AW into the write datum, B (the bus-idle third word), IY stepped, a word with no act, Y (the request word), two words with no act, the write's post, E bus-idle on the write's first clock (G N, Q23)"
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the destination's address IY
    ra=AW d1=OPRW s1=RA                     ; AW (AL) into the write datum
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 11) B: the bus-idle third word
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IY + the width
    wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IY stepped
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the write due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act (WO46: the ee word after it was the shared delay's word)
    ee                                      ; ee (WO46): the early end: with RAMEN 0 this word is E, the word after it the dispatch
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1                        ; post the write (Y + 3)
    e ro bi                                 ; E: (Q23) G N: the next opcode released on the write cycle's first clock (bus-idle); an on-chip store holds it to the write's end (RAMEN)

routine ldm op=AC,AD book="LDM" diff=0 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) LDM is `. . . . Y DN .` (the qprobe ldmb / ldmw runs): the source's address, three words with no act, Y (the request word: the read due four clocks after it), IX stepped under the wait, the read's post, F with E (D N)"
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the source's address IX
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 22, spec 18 B, Q102) B: LODS's bus-idle third word (`. . B . Y DN .`)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IX + the width
    wr=IX ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IX stepped
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                        ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f wr=AW ws=OPR e ro                     ; D N: F: the datum into AW (AL); E; ro: released

routine cmpm op=AE,AF book="CMPM" width=word diff=0 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) CMPM is `. . . . . . Y D . . N . .` (the qprobe cmpm runs): the destination's address, five words with no act, Y, IY stepped under the wait, the read's post, F (D), the compare, a word with no act, the next opcode released (N), E a word later"
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the destination's address IY
    open call=sb4                           ; OPEN: (r25, work order 21 B4, Q121) five words, the fourth bus-idle (`. . . B . . Y`: zz_late.uasm sb4)
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IY + the width
    wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IY stepped
    bus=MEMR seg=DS1                        ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f d1=TA s1=OPR                          ; D: F: the datum into tmpa
    ra=AW alu=GRP ax=RA ay=TA wf            ; the compare AW - [IY] (W)
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    ro                                      ; N: the next opcode released
    e                                       ; E, a word after the release

routine inm op=6C,6D bookx="19+2W" diff=1 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) INM is `. . . . . X D Z DN .` (the qprobe inm runs): the port DW, four words with no act, X (the I/O request word: the slot), the destination's address, IY stepped, the I/O read's post, F (D), the write's post (Z: the datum + 2), F with E (D N: the write's end)"
    ra=DW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the port DW into the address register
    open call=sb5                           ; OPEN: (r25, work order 21 B4, Q121) four words, the fifth of the routine bus-idle (`. . . . B X`: zz_late.uasm sb5)
    rl=x                                    ; (qprobe round 11) X: the I/O request word (waits while the bus unit's slot is taken; the cycle four clocks after it)
    ra=IY wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IY + the width
    open                                    ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) a word with no act
    bus=IOR                                 ; post the I/O read (X + 3)
    f d1=OPRW s1=OPR                        ; D: F: the port's datum into the write datum
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the destination's address IY
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1                        ; Z: post the write (the datum + 2; the format's width)
    f wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD e ro            ; D N: F: the write's end; IY stepped; E; ro: released

routine outm op=6E,6F bookx="19+2W" diff=2 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q34) OUTM is `. . . . . . Y D . X . . . N .` (the qprobe outmb / outmw runs): the source's address, five words with no act, Y, IX stepped, the read's post, F (D), the port DW, X (the I/O request word, two after the datum), two words with no act, the I/O write's post (X + 3), E"
    ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the source's address IX
    open call=w2                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) three words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 2)
    bi                                      ; (qprobe round 20, spec 16 B, Q90) B: OUTM's bus-idle fifth word (`. . . . B . Y D . X . . . N .`)
    open                                    ; OPEN: a word with no act
    rl=x bi                                 ; (qprobe round 11) Y: the request word (the read due four clocks after it, posted three words later)
    ra=IX wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA           ; SIGMA = IX + the width
    wr=IX ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IX stepped
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                        ; post the read (Y + 3)
    f d1=OPRW s1=OPR                        ; D: F: the datum into the write datum
    ra=DW wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA            ; the port DW into the address register
    rl=x                                    ; (qprobe round 11) X: the I/O request word (the slot)
    open call=w1                            ; OPEN: (qprobe round 11) two words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 1)
    bus=IOW                                 ; post the I/O write (X + 3)
    e ro                                    ; E (N); ro: released

; ---- the REP forms. c2 the prefix's word (SIGMA = CW), c3 the zero test; the elements from q
; ---- (qprobe round 11, Q35) the REP forms: the prefix's word (c2, CW into SIGMA), the zero test
; (c3: the prefix's own two words, the model's), then the string routine's words from c4: a head
; (14 words, the fourth bus-idle; INM / OUTM the fifth, OUTM 15 words), CW iterations that wait
; for their own cycles (Y / X request words, F the datum or the write's end), the tail. The first
; iteration is entered past the take point; every later one starts on its take point (the previous
; element done: its cycles, the index steps, CW written, the count's test), so an interrupt is
; taken between elements only (F5e). CW = 0: rep_z, `. . . B . . . . . . N .`.
routine rep_z why="OPEN: a REP form with CW = 0 (no element): c4 on, E at c17 (the memory forms), c18 (INM / OUTM: the port's word first); the frozen model's zexit (F24-out-r-rep-*-n0-pE-w0 S-to-S 17 / 18); (qprobe round 11) Q35's `. . . B . . . . . . N .` from c4 was built and lost ten round-9 runs (r*0 at pO, W = 2: the prefix's boundary waits, not made here): kept as it was"
rz_iox: open                                ; OPEN: (qprobe round 22, spec 18 B, Q102) REP INM / OUTM with CW = 0 is `. . . . B . . . . . . N .` (12 words, the bus-idle fifth; QPr21f r{inm,outm}w0): c6, one word more in front of the bus-idle word
rz_io: open                                 ; OPEN: (qprobe round 12, spec 7 A3) CW = 0 is `. . . B . . . . . . N .` behind the prefix (every form; the qprobe r*0 runs): c6, a word with no act
rz_m: bi call=w6                            ; B: the bus-idle fourth word (c7); OPEN: c8 .. c13 (the call and the shared delay's 6)
    e ro                                    ; E: pop the next opcode (c14); ro: released

; (WO47, round 4) REP MOVBK and REP STM on one body for both modes (the second bodies rm0 / rs0 of round 2 are gone):
; the access wait and the datum wait (fa / f), the write as a mode post one word later with RAMEN 0 (p1 / p0), the count's
; test on the write's RAMEN 1 post word (the last element leaves the loop there: its write one word later still), one
; word and a bus-idle word in front of the exit's delay. Every count of words here is read from the pins.
routine rep_movbk op=A4,A5 page=rep bookx="2+16+(18+2W)n" n=4 diff=4 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q35) REP MOVBK: the head (14 words from c4, B the fourth), the iteration `Y D . . . Z D .` (18 + the cycles' waits), the tail `. . . . . . N .` (the qprobe rmovb / rmovw, r11c runs; F24-out-r-rep-movbk-w-n2-pE-w0) (WO47 round 4, build/overseer/ramen-design4 DESIGN4.md; one body for both settings, user ruling 2026-11-24) OPEN at RAMEN 0, word counts read from the pins: the element's write posted one word later (p1 / p0: 1 word), the last element's two words later (2 words), the read's F an access wait (fa) with the datum taken on the word in front of the post; the exit one word and a bus-idle word in front of the five-word delay. OPEN at RAMEN 1: the exit's bus-idle word (it was a word with no act; it can wait for a fetch's pin cycle, which no window or corpus run shows); why silicon has these words is not known"
    ra=CW rb=IX wid=WORD alu=PASS ax=RA d1=ADDR s1=RB ; c4 ((qprobe round 12, spec 7 A3): the prefix's two words are its own routine, rep_p: c2 c3): SIGMA = CW (the count's test); the first source address IX
    jnc=SNZ:rz_io                           ; c5: CW = 0: no element (rep_z)
    open                                    ; OPEN: c6, the head's word with no act
    bi call=w10                             ; B: the head's bus-idle fourth word (c7); OPEN: c8 .. c17 (the call and the shared delay's 10)
    rl=x bi jmp=rmv_b                       ; Y: the first element's request word (c18; no take point before the first element)
rmv_y: ra=IX wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA rl=x bi tki=rep_brk ; Y: the next element's request word, its source address IX; (F5e) the take point (the previous element done)
rmv_b: ra=IX wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA         ; Y + 1: SIGMA = IX + the width
    wr=IX ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; Y + 2: IX stepped (written back before the read's datum is taken: a source over the on-chip RAM reads its own IX slot stepped, silicon f3_bins / the fuzz snapshots)
    bus=MEMR seg=DSP                        ; Y + 3: post the source read
    fa                                      ; (WO47, round 4) the access wait (RAMEN 1): the datum is taken four words on
    ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA alu=STEP ax=RA ; the destination's address IY; SIGMA = IY + the width
    wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD                   ; IY stepped (before the write: STM / INM / MOVBK over IY's own slot)
    ra=CW wid=WORD alu=DEC ax=RA            ; SIGMA = CW - 1
    f d1=OPRW s1=OPR                        ; (WO47, round 4) F: the datum wait, on the word that takes the datum: into the write datum (was a word with no act)
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 p1 jnc=SNZ:rep_l       ; Z: post the destination write with RAMEN 1 (the datum + 5); the count's test: CW - 1 = 0 is the last element
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 p0                     ; (WO47, round 4) p0: the write posted here with RAMEN 0 (one word later); with RAMEN 1 a word under the write
    f wr=CW ws=SIG wid=WORD                 ; D: F: the write's end (RAMEN 1); CW written
    jmp=rmv_y                               ; the next element

routine rep_stm op=AA,AB page=rep bookx="2+16+(9+W)n" n=4 diff=4 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q35) REP STM: the head (14 words, B the fourth), the iteration `Y D .` (9 + the write's waits), the tail `. . . . . . N .` (the qprobe rstmw, r11c runs; F24-out-r-rep-stm-w-n2-pE-w0) (WO47 round 4, build/overseer/ramen-design4 DESIGN4.md; one body for both settings, user ruling 2026-11-24) OPEN at RAMEN 0, word counts read from the pins: the element's write posted one word later (p1 / p0: 1 word), the last element's two words later (2 words), the count's test on the RAMEN 1 post word; the exit one word and a bus-idle word in front of the five-word delay. OPEN at RAMEN 1: the exit's bus-idle word (it was a word with no act; it can wait for a fetch's pin cycle, which no window or corpus run shows); why silicon has these words is not known"
    ra=CW rb=IY wid=WORD alu=PASS ax=RA d1=ADDR s1=RB ; c4 ((qprobe round 12, spec 7 A3): the prefix is rep_p, c2 c3): SIGMA = CW; the first destination address IY
    jnc=SNZ:rz_io                           ; c5: CW = 0: no element (rep_z) ((work order 26) the write datum's load moved to c6: L40 has no room for a register read, a payload and a target in one word)
    ra=AW d1=OPRW s1=RA                     ; c6: AW (AL) into the write datum ((work order 26) from c5; the datum is first used by the element's write, c18 + 3)
    bi call=w10                             ; B: the head's bus-idle fourth word (c7); OPEN: c8 .. c17 (the call and the shared delay's 10)
    rl=x bi jmp=rst_b                       ; Y: the first element's request word (c18)
rst_y: ra=IY wid=WORD d1=ADDR s1=RA rl=x bi tki=rep_brk ; Y: the next element's request word, its address IY; (F5e) the take point
rst_b: ra=IY wid=WORD alu=STEP ax=RA        ; Y + 1: SIGMA = IY + the width
    ra=CW wr=IY ws=SIG wid=WORD alu=DEC ax=RA ; Y + 2: IY stepped; SIGMA = CW - 1
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 p1 jnc=SNZ:rep_l       ; Y + 3: post the write with RAMEN 1; the count's test: CW - 1 = 0 is the last element
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 p0                     ; (WO47, round 4) p0: the write posted here with RAMEN 0 (one word later); with RAMEN 1 a word under the write
    f wr=CW ws=SIG wid=WORD                 ; D: F: the write's end (RAMEN 1); CW written
    jmp=rst_y                               ; the next element
; the last element's words (both routines): with RAMEN 1 its write is posted (the word that jumped here) and these run under it
rep_l: open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47, round 4) a word under the write (with RAMEN 1 it runs inside the cycle, in front of F's wait)
    bus=MEMW seg=DS1 p0                     ; (WO47, round 4) p0: the last write posted here with RAMEN 0 (two words later than RAMEN 1's)
    f wr=CW ws=SIG wid=WORD                 ; D: F: the write's end (RAMEN 1); CW written
    open                                    ; OPEN: (WO47, round 4) a word with no act (with RAMEN 0 it is absorbed by the bus-idle word's wait for the write's end)
    bi                                      ; B: bus-idle: with RAMEN 0 the exit waits here for the last write's end; with RAMEN 1 the write has ended
    open call=w4                            ; OPEN: the tail's five words with no act (the call and the shared delay's 4)
    e ro                                    ; E (N); ro: released

routine rep_ldm op=AC,AD page=rep bookx="2+16+(11+W)n" n=4 diff=5 why="OPEN: silicon longer than the book (measured, the extra words OPEN): (qprobe round 11, Q35) REP LDM: the head (14 words, B the fourth), the iteration `Y D . . .` (11 + the read's waits), the tail `. . . . . . . N .` (the qprobe rldmw, r11c runs; F24-out-r-rep-ldm-w-n2-pE-w0)"
